    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9561" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">compendĭo</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		compendium (eccl. Lat.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To shorten</i>, <i>abridge</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sermonem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4, 1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Compendiare alicui, lit., <i>to
				shorten the way of life for one;</i> hence, <i>to
				kill him</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug. Quaest. in Hept. 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
